  "rescue_truck_step_3_detail": "Use the built-in steps/handles on the cab. Don't pull on door handles to climb — they may break.",
  "rescue_truck_step_4_title": "Check driver consciousness",
  "rescue_truck_step_4_detail": "Tap and call out. Driver may be trapped by steering wheel. Do NOT force them out.",
  "rescue_truck_step_5_title": "Extraction needs 3+ people",
  "rescue_truck_step_5_detail": "One holds head/neck, two support body. Lower driver down cab steps slowly. Never drop.",
  "rescue_truck_step_6_title": "Move victim 50m away",
  "rescue_truck_step_6_detail": "Trucks carry large fuel loads. Move victim far from vehicle in case of fire.",
  "rescue_truck_firstaid_1": "🚨 Call 108 AND fire brigade (101) — truck fires spread fast.",
  "rescue_truck_firstaid_2": "🩸 Truck drivers often hit steering wheel — check chest for injury.",
  "rescue_truck_firstaid_3": "👁️ Check for head injuries — helmet-less impact with windshield is common.",
  "rescue_truck_firstaid_4": "🦺 If cargo has hazmat symbols, stay back and call 112.",
  "rescue_bike_type": "Motorcycle / Bike / Scooter",
  "rescue_bike_desc": "Two-wheeler, rider likely thrown from vehicle",
  "rescue_bike_danger_1": "⛽ Small fuel tank near engine — can ignite easily",
  "rescue_bike_danger_2": "🪖 DO NOT remove helmet — may cause spinal damage",
  "rescue_bike_danger_3": "🛣️ Rider likely skidded — check for road rash injuries",
  "rescue_bike_danger_4": "🔥 Hot exhaust pipe — avoid touching, can cause burns",
  "rescue_bike_step_1_title": "Move the bike away first",
  "rescue_bike_step_1_detail": "The bike is the fire risk. Push it at least 10m away from the victim before helping.",
  "rescue_bike_step_2_title": "NEVER remove the helmet",
  "rescue_bike_step_2_detail": "Even if victim asks. Helmet removal can cause fatal spinal damage. Only doctors should remove it.",
  "rescue_bike_step_3_title": "Check breathing through visor",
  "rescue_bike_step_3_detail": "Open the visor to check breathing. If vomiting, hold helmet steady and gently tilt to side.",
  "rescue_bike_step_4_title": "Check for road rash",
  "rescue_bike_step_4_detail": "Large skin abrasions from skidding. Cover with clean cloth — don't clean with water yet.",
  "rescue_bike_step_5_title": "Keep rider still and flat",
  "rescue_bike_step_5_detail": "Riders are often thrown and land awkwardly. Assume spinal injury. Keep them flat until help arrives.",
  "rescue_bike_step_6_title": "Keep them warm",
  "rescue_bike_step_6_detail": "Shock causes rapid body cooling. Cover with jacket/blanket. Keep talking to them.",
  "rescue_bike_firstaid_1": "🪖 NEVER remove helmet — this is the most important rule for bike accidents.",
  "rescue_bike_firstaid_2": "🦴 Assume broken limbs — don't try to straighten or move them.",
  "rescue_bike_firstaid_3": "😮 Shock is common — keep victim lying down, legs slightly elevated.",
  "rescue_bike_firstaid_4": "🩸 Road rash bleeds a lot but is rarely life-threatening — focus on head/spine.",
  "rescue_ev_car_type": "Electric Vehicle (EV Car)",
  "rescue_ev_car_desc": "Battery-powered car — special electrical hazards",
  "rescue_ev_car_danger_1": "⚡ HIGH VOLTAGE battery (400-800V) — can be LETHAL if touched",
  "rescue_ev_car_danger_2": "🔥 Lithium battery fires burn at 1000°C and CANNOT be extinguished easily",
  "rescue_ev_car_danger_3": "🌊 If EV is in water — stay away, electric shock risk is EXTREME",
  "rescue_ev_car_danger_4": "💨 Battery fires release toxic gases — stay upwind",
  "rescue_ev_car_danger_5": "🔄 Car may still be \"on\" even if silent — EVs make no engine noise",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_1_title": "DO NOT touch orange cables",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_1_detail": "Orange cables carry high voltage. If you see orange wires exposed — do NOT touch the car at all.",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_2_title": "Turn off the car",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_2_detail": "If safe, reach in and press power button. Look for emergency cut-off switch (usually near door sill — bright red/orange).",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_3_title": "Check for battery damage",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_3_detail": "If battery area (under floor) is visibly damaged or smoking — treat as fire emergency. Move victim 30m away.",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_4_title": "Extraction same as regular car",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_4_detail": "Once confirmed safe (no exposed cables, no smoke), extraction steps are same as regular car. Support neck, slide out.",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_5_title": "If battery catches fire — RUN",
  "rescue_ev_car_step_5_detail": "EV battery fires cannot be put out with normal extinguishers. Move everyone 50m away and call fire brigade 101.",
  "rescue_ev_car_firstaid_1": "⚡ If victim received electric shock: do not touch them until power is confirmed off.",
  "rescue_ev_car_firstaid_2": "👁️ Electric shock victims may have internal burns not visible outside.",
  "rescue_ev_car_firstaid_3": "🫁 Toxic battery fumes — move victim upwind, fresh air is critical.",
  "rescue_ev_car_firstaid_4": "🚒 Always call fire brigade for EV accidents — even if no visible fire yet.",
  "rescue_bus_type": "Bus / Minibus",
  "rescue_bus_desc": "Large passenger vehicle, multiple victims likely",
  "rescue_bus_danger_1": "👥 Multiple casualties — prioritize who needs help most (triage)",
  "rescue_bus_danger_2": "⛽ Large fuel tank — fire risk is HIGH",
  "rescue_bus_danger_3": "💨 CNG buses have gas cylinders — EXPLOSION RISK if ruptured",
  "rescue_bus_danger_4": "🚪 Emergency exits at rear and roof — know how to use them",
  "rescue_bus_step_1_title": "Assess from outside first",
  "rescue_bus_step_1_detail": "Count visible victims. Check for fire/smoke. Don't rush in — a second casualty helps no one.",
  "rescue_bus_step_2_title": "Check for CNG cylinders",
  "rescue_bus_step_2_detail": "CNG buses have cylindrical tanks on roof or rear. If hissing sound heard — evacuate everyone 100m away immediately.",
  "rescue_bus_step_3_title": "Use emergency exits",
  "rescue_bus_step_3_detail": "Red handles at rear door and roof hatch. Push/pull to open. Don't wait for front door if jammed.",
  "rescue_bus_step_4_title": "Triage victims — most critical first",
  "rescue_bus_step_4_detail": "Walking wounded can help themselves. Focus on unconscious or heavily bleeding victims first.",
  "rescue_bus_step_5_title": "Form human chain for extraction",
  "rescue_bus_step_5_detail": "Line up bystanders to pass victims out of windows/exits. One person stabilizes head, others support body.",
  "rescue_bus_firstaid_1": "📞 Call 108 AND 100 — multiple casualties need multiple ambulances.",
  "rescue_bus_firstaid_2": "🏃 Get able-bodied passengers out first — they can then help others.",
  "rescue_bus_firstaid_3": "🔴 Triage: Red = critical (help first), Yellow = serious, Green = walking.",
  "rescue_bus_firstaid_4": "💨 If CNG leak suspected — NO flames, NO phones near the vehicle.",
  "rescue_auto_type": "Auto Rickshaw / Tuk-Tuk",
